"comparison": "Both Goldman Sachs and Morgan Stanley disclose that new business initiatives and expansions expose them to enhanced regulatory, reputational, credit, and operational risks. Specifically, MS notes these activities 'expose us to new and enhanced risks, greater regulatory scrutiny... increased credit-related, sovereign, compliance and operational risks, as well as franchise and reputational concerns' (ms_2024_1A_P116_S002), mirroring GS's disclosure that 'New business initiatives expose us to new and enhanced risks, including... reputational concerns... greater regulatory scrutiny... increased credit-related, market, sovereign and operational risks' (gs_2024_1A_P206_S001). Both firms identify reputational harm and regulatory scrutiny as key consequences of pursuing new business lines.",
