"relationship": "related_topic",
"comparison": "While Goldman Sachs focuses on the execution risks of acquisitions and new business initiatives, Morgan Stanley links its 'integration of acquisitions and other strategic initiatives' directly to heightened cybersecurity and operational risks. GS warns that failure to successfully execute initiatives can lead to 'unanticipated costs and losses' and 'negative reputational effects' (gs_2024_1A_P207_S002), whereas MS states that integration of acquisitions and strategic initiatives may 'subject us to new technology, customers or third-party providers' which heightens risks that could result in 'cyberattack... or result in disclosure or misuse of personal, confidential or proprietary information' (ms_2024_1A_P033_S003). Both identify acquisitions as a vector for introducing new risk profiles, though MS highlights the specific cyber/operational angle while GS highlights broader execution and financial risk.",
