"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both Goldman Sachs and JPMorgan Chase identify the ability to effectively integrate acquired businesses as a critical determinant of success for strategic initiatives. GS states, 'The success of our acquisitions will depend, in part, on our ability to integrate the acquired businesses and realize anticipated synergies, cost savings and growth opportunities' (gs_2024_1A_P210_S003). Similarly, JPMorgan lists 'effectively integrate newly-acquired businesses' as a key management effectiveness factor that, if failed, could adversely affect strategic objectives (jpm_2024_1A_P168_S010). Both firms explicitly frame integration capability as a core risk factor in their M&A and new business strategies.",
