"comparison": "Both Goldman Sachs and Citi highlight that new business initiatives and strategic investments carry execution risks that can lead to higher-than-expected expenses and negative financial impacts. GS warns that failure to execute initiatives may result in 'unanticipated costs and losses' (gs_2024_1A_P207_S002). Citi similarly states that its simplification and investment initiatives 'involve various execution challenges, may take longer than expected and may result in higher than expected expenses... and other negative financial or strategic impacts' (c_2024_1A_P022_S003). Both disclosures emphasize that the complexity and uncertainty of these strategic moves can materially impact financial results.",
